this protest in Seattle Washington on  June 1st looks to be contained but in a  split second everything unravels since  the killing of George Floyd police  departments across the country are  facing increased scrutiny over their  tactics this incident in Seattle's  Capitol Hill neighborhood is under  investigation by the police departments  internal watchdog group for the use of  pepper spray blast balls and tear gas to  disperse a crowd The Wall Street Journal  analyzed over two hours of footage shot  by multiple witnesses as well as police  scanner audio from the scene to examine  how police and protesters tactics pushed  the incident into chaos an hour after a  citywide curfew about 2,000 people are  headed east on Pine Street toward the  Seattle police East precinct to protest  [Applause]  but Seattle PD quickly erected a barrier  one block away the scene still seems  under control the precinct captain even  listens and responds to protest our  demands the tone changes when an  organizer warns that some people have  other tactics in mind  this boy  Wow overloaded control then a crucial  change in police tactics they swapped  the line of bike officers for officers  in riot gear they also discussed using  pepper spray what they refer to as OSE  short for oleoresin capsicum then a  change in tactics from some protesters a  few at the front begin raising umbrellas  which protesters frequently used to  shield themselves from pepper spray and  tear gas police experts we spoke with  note that umbrellas are often seen as a  hazard because they block sight lines  then the pivotal moment a person in  front is holding an umbrella that  extends to past the barricade an officer  reaches out attempting to push it out of  the way the officer grabs the umbrella  and the person tries to hold on at the  same time another officer deploys pepper  spray at the direction of the incident  commander or I see other officers follow  suit spraying as the crowd backs away  some in the crowd they're objects toward  the police line then the order to deploy  blasts falls in CS or tear gas  [Music]  most of the protesters have dispersed at  this point but if you remain close to  the barrier despite to your guts filling  the air Seattle Police Department policy  dictates that once a crowd poses an  imminent risk to public safety or  property destruction police should give  in order to disperse the policy also  states officers will not use blast balls  until a dispersal order has been issued  footage we reviewed didn't show officers  giving a verbal order the Seattle Police  Department said the incident is still  under investigation police declare the  June 1st protest a riot because some  people in the crowd threw objects at  police 11 people were arrested according  to seattle police 12 people required  medical attention including police and  members of the public
 

